# Build context for the relay's Docker image (see Dockerfile) — deny
# everything, then allow back in exactly what `go build` needs. Without
# this, the whole repo (docs/, webspace/, README, and — biggest — the full
# .git history) gets sent to the Docker daemon and copied into the build
# stage on every single build, which does two bad things: it's slower to
# transfer, and it makes the Docker layer cache unstable — a change to
# docs/app.js alone would invalidate the COPY . . layer and force a full
# recompile, even though nothing Go-related changed.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!main.go
!internal
!internal/**
